  On the one hand, this isn't a new problem.  Save scumming has 
been around for years.  On the other hand, save scumming isn't 
possible on a server.

  The judo approach: sometimes the only way to win is by giving 
in.  Misfot has used this approach for years.  Adding a web
browser, phone dialer, etc.

  The only real difference between Nethack and other games is the
"House of Cards" effect.  I.e.:  Die and you lose everything.  No
restore of any kind, except save scumming.

  That's why these "Surprise, you're dead!" kind of things are so
annoying.  If cruel deaths were really the problem then the 
original Doom would never have become popular.

  (I've seen people complain that some Final Fantasy game could 
only be saved in a town/inn.  There was some part of the game 
where they kept dying over and over.  They found redoing the 
part from the last save to be particularly annoying.)

  So a) encourage use of Explore mode for newbies.

     b) Add a "Trainer" mode.  Like explore mode you get the 
        option of resurrection after every death.  The number 
        of resurrections is recorded in the score file.  The 
        final score is divided by 2 raised to the power of the
        number of resurrections.  Resurrect twice, score/4.  
        Resurrect 10 times, score/1024.  Ascend without dying:
        permanent firestorm of controversy in rgrn.

     c) Trainer mode 2:  Allow "perma-saves" in attended temples.
        Costs so many zorkmids per XP level.  Only guaranteed
        attended temples remain the mines and VotD.  Number of
        perma-saves and uses thereof recorded separately in log 
        file, with some appropriate effect on score.

  Trainer mode 2 looks best.  A "too-old" perma-save is more 
trouble than it's worth.  (Look at Krysia's Krusader.  When the
pet disaster happened the game could have been continued from
an old system backup.  A backup KK decided was too old for his
purposes.)

  Perma-saves look like a save-scummers dream: acceptance at 
last.  But there's a big difference between saving/restoring 
where ever you like, and only doing so in an attended temple.
And it takes zorkmids.

